    "proof_tex": "The already established exact accounting theorem states\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\nR_{n,m}(\\delta_m,\\beta)-R_n^{\\mathrm{or}}(\\beta)\n&=d_{T_n^{\\mathrm{full}}}(\\beta)\n-\\left(\\frac Nn\\right)^2\nE_{S_m}d_{T_{n,m}^{\\mathrm{main}}}(\\beta)\\\\\n&\\quad+\n\\left(\\frac Nn\\right)^2E\\!\\left[\nV_{T_{n,m}^{\\mathrm{main}}}(\\delta_m,\\beta)\n-V_{T_{n,m}^{\\mathrm{main}}}\n\\{G_{T_{n,m}^{\\mathrm{main}}}(\\beta),\\beta\\}\n\\right].\n\\end{aligned}\n\\tag{30}\n\\]\nThe first line on the right of (30) is \\(D_{n,m}(\\beta)\\), and the second line is \\(L_{n,m}(\\delta_m,\\beta)\\), by\n\\(\\mathrm{def{:}exact\\text{-}risk\\text{-}components}\\).  This proves the exact identity.\n\nFor \\(\\delta_m=\\widehat G_m\\), subtract\n\\(A(\\beta)m/n^2+B(\\beta)/(nm)\\) from both sides of (30).  The resulting equality is\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n&R_{n,m}(\\widehat G_m,\\beta)-R_n^{\\mathrm{or}}(\\beta)\n-A(\\beta)\\frac m{n^2}-\\frac{B(\\beta)}{nm}\\\\\n&\\quad=\n\\left\\{D_{n,m}(\\beta)-A(\\beta)\\frac m{n^2}\\right\\}\n+\\left\\{L_{n,m}(\\widehat G_m,\\beta)-\\frac{B(\\beta)}{nm}\\right\\}.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\tag{31}\n\\]\nDivision by the positive number\n\\(s_{n,m}=m/n^2+1/(nm)\\), followed by the supremum over the compact parameter set, proves the stated equivalence.  Equation (31) also shows why separate component estimates imply the expansion by the triangle inequality, and why the converse would be false without excluding cancellation.  Finally, for any class \\(\\mathcal D_m\\) of pilot-measurable actions and any parameter set \\(\\mathcal H\\subseteq\\mathcal K\\), (30) gives the identity\n\\[\n\\inf_{\\delta_m\\in\\mathcal D_m}\\sup_{\\beta\\in\\mathcal H}\n\\{R_{n,m}(\\delta_m,\\beta)-R_n^{\\mathrm{or}}(\\beta)\\}\n=\n\\inf_{\\delta_m\\in\\mathcal D_m}\\sup_{\\beta\\in\\mathcal H}\n\\{D_{n,m}(\\beta)+L_{n,m}(\\delta_m,\\beta)\\}.\n\\tag{32}\n\\]\nThus lower-bound statements are transferred by equality, not by an unproved sign claim about \\(L_{n,m}\\).  Equations (30)--(32) prove the reduction and the absence of a third term.",
    "justification": "The exact decomposition is the valid replacement for the unsupported uniform second-order theorem.",
    "gap": "Both coefficient-level component comparisons remain open.",
    "consumer": "It gives a precise checklist for validating a proposed pilot rule without introducing a hidden cross-wave term.",
